a36bb1f3","ma-c-2594704bf736a0bab0ea","ma-c-2d9b354134df65d7275d","ma-c-2f438091b20513108c07","ma-c-30c5a22ad40aa08ed3c8","ma-c-393dd89ff3f67053e7c3","ma-c-3cb27e5e107ed3505c66","ma-c-4caa2d41d14dc9abc85b","ma-c-5343def07b63e8d7ced8","ma-c-64c6f7dfbc85fe4c43c5","ma-c-6539d8db5f349d1972de","ma-c-6a92ef214f1f0e8af926","ma-c-6d53c272d9dc459f4db7","ma-c-711f416a195300af18df","ma-c-77f57dee48c6d17c008c","ma-c-7ec172a4edc4376d87cc","ma-c-8fc1e0355a7f0fae2bd6","ma-c-93054fd37cbd8392a304","ma-c-93eb5c03bac1508d16c6","ma-c-b8171910ec8c4207729a","ma-c-b8d7bc0df2d2205eff3b","ma-c-bae5376cb6753fe73d1c","ma-c-bdb398bdc60c4da31950","ma-c-c0e787a7d6f836a28cce","ma-c-c11655b2d19c311c7f9a","ma-c-c55aae40e7443fdab57b","ma-c-c9e7a565b1253273f387","ma-c-caefe74f53d2a807c021","ma-c-caf3eb13908bafb0b074","ma-c-d0082a45c7dfcfe4fdf1","ma-c-f4e1b63b164650742fc5","ma-c-f54df5f1593372c0aede","ma-c-fc88bb192b15a62a9309"],"papers":{"arXiv:1307.2941":{"abstract":"Let $\\hat{\\mathfrak g}$ be an affine Lie algebra of type 1. We give a PBW basis for the quantum affine algebra $U_q(\\hat{\\mathfrak g})$ with respect to the triangular decomposition of $\\hat{\\mathfrak g}$ associated with the imaginary positive root system.","authors":["Ben Cox","Vyacheslav Futorny","Kailash C. Misra"],"year":"2013"},"arXiv:0902.1273":{"abstract":"In this paper we construct two free field realizations of the elliptic affine Lie algebra sl(2,R) + Ω_R/dR, where R=C[t,t^{-1},u|u^2=t^3 - 2b t^2 + t]. The first realization gives an analogue of Wakimoto's construction for Affine Kac-Moody algebras, but in the setting of the elliptic affine Lie algebra. The second realization gives new type of representations analogous to Imaginary Verma modules i","authors":["Andre Bueno","Ben Cox","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2009"},"arXiv:2307.04306":{"abstract":"For an arbitrary affine Lie algebra we study an analog of the category O for the natural Borel subalgebra and zero central charge. We show that such category is semisimple having the reduced imaginary Verma modules as its simple objects. This generalizes the result of Cox, Futorny, Misra in the case of affine sl(2).","authors":["Juan Camilo Arias","Vyacheslav Futorny","André de Oliveira"],"year":"2023"},"arXiv:1107.0893":{"abstract":"We study $\\mathbb Z$-graded modules of nonzero level with arbitrary weight multiplicities over Heisenberg Lie algebras and the associated generalized loop modules over affine Kac-Moody Lie algebras. We construct new families of such irreducible modules over Heisenberg Lie algebras. Our main result establishes the irreducibility of the corresponding generalized loop modules providing an explicit co","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Georgia Benkart","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:1610.07973":{"abstract":"The goal of the present paper is to obtain new free field realizations of affine Kac-Moody algebras motivated by geometric representation theory for generalized flag manifolds of finite-dimensional semisimple Lie groups. We provide an explicit construction of a large class of irreducible modules associated with certain parabolic subalgebras covering all known special cases.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Libor Křižka","Petr Somberg"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:math/0601471":{"abstract":"We show that our construction of boson type realizations of affine $\\mathfrak{sl}(n+1)$ in terms of intermediate Wakimoto modules gives representations that are generically isomorphic to certain Verma type modules. We then use this identification to obtain information about the submodule structure of intermediate Wakimoto modules","authors":["Ben L. Cox","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2006"},"arXiv:1610.07082":{"abstract":"The main result of the paper establishes the irreducibility of a large family of nonzero central charge induced modules over Affine Lie algebras for any non standard parabolic subalgebra. It generalizes all previously known partial results and provides a a construction of many new irreducible modules.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Iryna Kashuba"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:math/0010322":{"abstract":"Let g be an untwisted affine Kac-Moody algebra and M_J(lambda) a Verma-type module for g with J-highest integral weight lambda. We construct quantum Verma-type modules M_J^q(lambda) over the quantum group U_q(g), investigate their properties and show that M_J^q(lambda) is a true quantum deformation of M_J(ł) in the sense that the weight structure is preserved under the deformation. We also analyze","authors":["Vyacheslav M. Futorny","Duncan J. Melville","Alexander N. Grishkov"],"year":"2000"},"arXiv:2002.05586":{"abstract":"We construct new families of positive energy representations of affine vertex algebras together with their free field realizations by using localization technique. We introduce the twisting functor T_αon the category of modules over affine Kac--Moody algebra \\widehat{g}_κof level κfor any positive root αof g, and the Wakimoto functor from a certain category of g-modules to the category of smooth \\","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Libor Křižka"],"year":"2020"},"arXiv:math/0104201":{"abstract":"We classify the derived tame Schur and infinitesimal Schur algebras and describe indecomposable objects in their derived categories.","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2001"},"arXiv:0711.0793":{"abstract":"We show that if A is an abelian category satisfying certain mild conditions, then one can introduce the concept of a moduli space of (semi)stable objects which has the structure of a projective algebraic variety. This idea is applied to several important abelian categories in representation theory, like highest weight categories.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Marcos Jardim","Adriano Moura"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0903.1062":{"abstract":"We consider imaginary Verma modules for quantum affine algebra $U_q(\\hat{\\mathfrak{sl}(2)})$ and construct Kashiwara type operators and the Kashiwara algebra $\\mathcal K_q$. We show that a certain quotient $\\mathcal N_q^-$ of $U_q(\\hat{\\mathfrak{sl}(2)})$ is a simple $\\mathcal K_q$-module.","authors":["Ben Cox","Vyacheslav Futorny","Kailash C. Misra"],"year":"2009"}}}